        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Prepared analogously to 5: Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (or the corresponding LnCl3 hydrate), hmpH and NaN3 were dissolved in MeCN, then hexanuclear manganese pivalate was added, followed by KOH crushed with a glass rod. The vial was closed except for one hole and stirred 40 min at 70 °C. The dark brown solution was cooled, filtered, and allowed to evaporate slowly. For the other lanthanides, DyCl3 hydrate (0.078 g, 0.2 mmol) was used in place of the nitrate and crystals formed in ten days; 1 used 0.074 g (0.20 mmol) SmCl3 hydrate in place of DyCl3 hydrate.",
